    const Section(
      title: '+ Outline your differential diagnosis and the targeted laboratory workup needed to exclude mimics of fibromyalgia.',
      content: '**Key Differential Diagnoses to Exclude**:\n\n1. **Hypothyroidism**: Fatigue, cognitive dysfunction, myalgias, and weight gain can all mimic fibromyalgia. Order **TSH and free T4**. Even subclinical hypothyroidism (elevated TSH with normal T4) can cause symptoms.\n\n2. **Inflammatory Arthritis (Rheumatoid Arthritis, SLE, Sjogren syndrome)**: Despite normal joint exam, early inflammatory arthritis may present with pain before visible synovitis. Order **ESR, CRP, ANA, RF, anti-CCP antibodies**. Sjogren syndrome is particularly important as it frequently coexists with fibromyalgia (ask about dry eyes and dry mouth).\n\n3. **Obstructive Sleep Apnea (OSA)**: Non-restorative sleep and fatigue are hallmarks of both. BMI 27.8 and cognitive dysfunction warrant screening. **STOP-BANG questionnaire** — if score >= 3, refer for polysomnography.\n\n4. **Vitamin D Deficiency**: Widespread musculoskeletal pain and fatigue. Extremely common and easily treatable. Order **25-hydroxyvitamin D level**.\n\n5. **Anemia**: Fatigue and cognitive changes. Order **CBC with differential**.\n\n6. **Hepatitis C**: Associated with widespread pain and fatigue. Order **Hepatitis C antibody** if risk factors present.\n\n7. **Multiple Sclerosis**: Fatigue, cognitive fog, and paresthesias in a middle-aged female. Her neurologic exam is normal, but this warrants consideration if symptoms progress.\n\n8. **Polymyalgia Rheumatica**: If patient were over 50 with elevated ESR. Less likely given age but worth considering.\n\n**Recommended Lab Panel**:\n- CBC with differential\n- Comprehensive metabolic panel (CMP)\n- TSH, free T4\n- ESR, CRP\n- ANA, RF, anti-CCP\n- 25-hydroxyvitamin D\n- HbA1c (diabetes can cause neuropathic pain)\n- Ferritin (iron deficiency can cause fatigue and restless legs)\n\n**Important**: Extensive additional testing (MRI of every painful area, EMG/NCS in the absence of neurologic deficits) is NOT recommended and can reinforce illness behavior and medicalization.',
